{
  "tema": 8565,
  "slug": "decir-contar",
  "titulo": "Decir vs contar (to tell)",
  "subtitulo": "Dime la hora / Cuéntame qué pasó.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Contar = to tell with details: a story, a joke, what happened. Decir = to say or tell a specific piece of information. In reported speech both work; contar sounds like news or gossip.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Verb",
            "Use",
            "Example"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "contar",
              "a story, joke, anecdote, what happened (details)",
              "Cuéntame cómo te fue."
            ],
            [
              "decir",
              "a specific piece of info, words, an order",
              "Dime a qué hora paso por ti."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In **reported speech**, both work: **me dijo que...** / **me contó que...** With **contar**, it sounds like news or juicy gossip."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Contar** is irregular (o → ue): **cuento, cuentas, cuenta**. **Decir**: **digo, dices, dice**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **contar** tells a story; **decir** tells a fact."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
